{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources","id":1516054,"title":"Thoughts regarding Neonates not exploiting crime to obtain power/resources?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-24T19:14:47-07:00","id":1516054,"title":"Thoughts regarding Neonates not exploiting crime to obtain power/resources?","content":"In VTM, a common trait is that the Elders have all the power/money and the young have none. My issue is that very few Neonates seem to capitalize on their inherent supernatural abilities to gain power/resources using crime.<br /> <br /> Presence and Dominate can be used quite easily to form a criminal organization/gang, force mortals into giving you what you want, and to scare mortals into not moving against you. Auspex can alert you to the movement of law enforcement and victims, as well as help you obtain important information like the code to the safe where jewelers keep their most valuable items. In fact, every discipline can be used in some way to easily commit crimes that mortals would have serious trouble pulling off.<br /> <br /> However, you almost never see neonates capitalizing on it.<br /> <br /> Why is that?\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T20:35:24-07:00","id":1516056,"title":"","content":"This might be an unpopular opinion but the key issue is the Players themselves. You can give a less than creative player all the mechanical advantages in a game and nothing will happen, but if you give a creative and somewhat unorthodox player a multi-tool, a flash drive, a smartphone and a data plan.... nations will fall. It takes a certain amount of either &quot;big picture&quot; thinking or &quot;outside the box&quot; thinking to create the sort of plans that will generate real power in a setting like VtM. Not all players have that or if they do, not everyone has the energy to plan such things after getting done with classes or their 9 to 5 job.<br /> <br /> For example, due to how much of an XP sink Thaumaturgy is, Tremere generally don't have functional power within a coterie until you pass the 75+ XP range, by that point most other PCs have more or less completed their build and are working on flavor stats or filling in gaps. So when I play a Tremere I usually have them use level 1 Auspex to hit up the local gambling dens and spend the evening playing against other gamblers rather than the house. In this way the Tremere basically became the bankroll for the coterie. Hit a different casino or den each night and you are looking at Resources 3 to 4 quite easily, and none of that is money that can be easily traced.<br /> <br /> But what do you do now that you have an untraceable monetary fund? Invest in properties so that your gambling money farms even more money, then purchase and upgrade multiple havens. So now you are the owners of multiple havens, own many businesses which generate passive income, you own controlling stock in corporations around the world, each member of the coterie is rated at Resources 5 individually.<br /> <br /> But now what? You have enough money to influence politics, manipulate the markets, hire mercenary companies, create entire fake companies to protect your interests or get you new toys. Power in the vampire world is a tricky thing because while you might have insane wealth, the humans you use are only could for a limited amount of time. If you ghouled the US president, at best they are only in power for 8 years, and anything you would want to have them do would have to be done carefully and quietly so they could only do you one or two favors in that time period.<br /> <br /> As you can see the scope can be grand, but due to the mechanics there is a degree of diminishing returns. Especially if the ST doesn't have a lot of storylines where you offer to pay off a neonates mortal families almost defaulted mortgage in exchange for them teaching you a rare discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T21:08:04-07:00","id":1516058,"title":"","content":"Now that I think about it, I have noticed that players seem to prefer going down the soap opera route instead of going big like robbing a jewel store, this is on the discord server I use anyway. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-24T22:20:52-07:00","id":1516062,"title":"","content":"Look, the excuse I was given was that any neonate that draws attention to itself suddenly tends to have a short unlife, either because it attracted hunters or interfered with an older kindred's business, either way I guess that could happen if an ST give players a chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T00:00:36-07:00","id":1516066,"title":"","content":"Creativity is indeed a key factor here<br /> (Or, I dare say, background knowledge, may God have mercy of the soul of a poor ST who have players with knowledge and background and let say path of conjuring or alchemy... )<br /> <br /> And of course the fact, Vampires rarely Embrace from that area of life - mostly to gain knowledge or influence from the said area - , and vampires inherently avoid unfamiliarty themselves and will not deepdive to learn the ins and outs of such things<br /> Not to mention, most of the vampires were... well... normal Humans. And we grew up learning Crime is a sin (if you come to a relegious background) or - obviously - against the Law<br /> Vampires were people, humans too, most often than not, good people, not criminals and part of the clinging to their Humanity is to try to behave like Humans and avoid thing humans would consider crime; murder, stealing, robbery, theft, burglary, arson (especially arson, Fire BAAAD), assault and abuse of any kind<br /> Neonates are - most of the time - try to remain Human and fit in to Humanity<br /> Sure, some of them jumps in the opportunity or were criminals to begin with, they obviously have an advantage, but I think if the vampire in question wasn't embraced exactly becasue she was already familiar wiht Crime, most of them will avoid it<br /> In time, thanks to the web of Gifts and Favors , aka &quot;Boons&quot; that tie the Cainite society together (Favors/Boons are the currency of the undead and agreeing to do or owe a favor is a big deal among vampires, even a neonate could and probably should and would eventually aquire a few) she will learn the nature of these things and slowly tries those with humans<br /> And the next step?<br /> Well, she will understand, when the Corleones make you an <i>offer</i> you <i>can't refuse</i>, you literally <i>can't refuse</i> it.<br /> It's a warning to do what <i>they</i> say, or else.<br /> <br /> Experience, paried with the slow errosion of Humanity will in time demolish those mental blocks that could prevent you to be a bad person and eventually you will come to a situation like this:<br /> <br /> Clara: You're scared.<br /> The Twelfth Doctor: I'm terrified.<br /> Clara: Of what?<br /> The Twelfth Doctor: The answer to my next question. Which must be honest, cold and considered without kindness or restraint. Clara, be my pal and tell me: am I a good man?<br /> Clara: I... don't know.<br /> The Twelfth Doctor: Neither do I.<br /> <br /> And<br /> <br /> Clara: I don't know.<br /> The Twelfth Doctor: 'm sorry?\u200b<br /> Clara: You asked me if you're a good man and the answer is, I don't know. But I think you try to be and I think that's probably the point.\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Usually when in my games we reach such or similar conversation even with a friend, ghoul, anyone or anything thats is the truning point<br /> Either the vampire continnue trying... or stops trying<br /> <br /> And good people will avoid crime like before... bad people?<br /> Well...<br /> <br /> The good are <i>innocent</i> and create justice. The bad are guilty, which is why they invent mercy.<br /> -Sir Terry Pratchett\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-25-2023, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T00:03:38-07:00","id":1516067,"title":"","content":"M'kay... so forum swallowed my post<br /> I hope one day it will be fixed and we could post and edit without fear<br /> Lets try again ,shall we?<br /> Okay<br /> <br /> Creativity is indeed a key factor here<br /> (Or, I dare say, background knowledge, may God have mercy of the soul of a poor ST who have players with knowledge and background and let say path of conjuring or alchemy... )<br /> <br /> And of course the fact, Vampires rarely Embrace from that area of life - mostly to gain knowledge or influence from the said area - , and vampires inherently avoid unfamiliarty themselves and will not deepdive to learn the ins and outs of such things<br /> Not to mention, most of the vampires were... well... normal Humans. And we grew up learning Crime is a sin (if you come to a relegious background) or - obviously - against the Law<br /> Vampires were people, humans too, most often than not, good people, not criminals and part of the clinging to their Humanity is to try to behave like Humans and avoid thing humans would consider crime; murder, stealing, robbery, theft, burglary, arson (especially arson, Fire BAAAD), assault and abuse of any kind<br /> Neonates are - most of the time - try to remain Human and fit in to Humanity<br /> Sure, some of them jumps in the opportunity or were criminals to begin with, they obviously have an advantage, but I think if the vampire in question wasn't embraced exactly becasue she was already familiar wiht Crime, most of them will avoid it<br /> In time, thanks to the web of Gifts and Favors , aka &quot;Boons&quot; that tie the Cainite society together (Favors/Boons are the currency of the undead and agreeing to do or owe a favor is a big deal among vampires, even a neonate could and probably should and would eventually aquire a few) she will learn the nature of these things and slowly tries those with humans<br /> And the next step?<br /> Well, she will understand, when the Corleones make you an <i>offer</i> you <i>can't refuse</i>, you literally <i>can't refuse</i> it.<br /> It's a warning to do what <i>they</i> say, or else.<br /> <br /> Experience, paried with the slow errosion of Humanity will in time demolish those mental blocks that could prevent you to be a bad person and eventually you will come to a situation like this:<br /> <br /> Clara: You're scared.<br /> The Twelfth Doctor: I'm terrified.<br /> Clara: Of what?<br /> The Twelfth Doctor: The answer to my next question. Which must be honest, cold and considered without kindness or restraint. Clara, be my pal and tell me: am I a good man?<br /> Clara: I... don't know.<br /> The Twelfth Doctor: Neither do I.<br /> <br /> And<br /> <br /> Clara: I don't know.<br /> The Twelfth Doctor: 'm sorry?\u200b<br /> Clara: You asked me if you're a good man and the answer is, I don't know. But I think you try to be and I think that's probably the point.\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Usually when in my games we reach such or similar conversation even with a friend, ghoul, anyone or anything thats is the truning point<br /> Either the vampire continnue trying... or stops trying<br /> <br /> And good people will avoid crime like before... bad people?<br /> Well...<br /> <br /> The good are <i>innocent</i> and create justice. The bad are guilty, which is why they invent mercy.<br /> -Sir Terry Pratchett\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T00:46:02-07:00","id":1516069,"title":"","content":"I've done it. I can think of many reasons why it's not the go-to<br /> <br /> 1-We're talking about blue collar crime here right? White collar crime is just better. Safer, invisible, more lucrative etc.. <br /> 2-Dealing with criminals exposes you to a lot more risk. Both in that they can try to kill you or in that you might wake up to find half your organization arrested and police looking for you. <br /> 3-Large Criminal organizations will operate beyond the scope of the kindred's domain and other vampires will not appreciate your agents in their territory. With smaller groups, given gang rivalries, dealing with criminals will earn you the ire of other vampires who may also be involved in criminal doings.<br /> 4-A lot of big money items like drugs or human traficking require complicated networks.<br /> 5-Big Mafias have their own internal hunter teams because they're aware of the BS. <br /> 6-Camarilla Kindred don't want to look aggressive or ambitious. They're the sect that promotes quiet friendly gatherings, peace and prosperity, and the road of humanity. Most don't want to befriend a thug they can't control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T02:20:29-07:00","id":1516075,"title":"","content":"I played a chopper/omar style stick up artist who used fortitude to deal with the occasional gun fight my malkavian partner used obfuscate to conceal just who was doing the robbery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T03:15:52-07:00","id":1516082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1516069#post1516069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've done it. I can think of many reasons why it's not the go-to<br /> <br /> 1-We're talking about blue collar crime here right? White collar crime is just better. Safer, invisible, more lucrative etc..<br /> 2-Dealing with criminals exposes you to a lot more risk. Both in that they can try to kill you or in that you might wake up to find half your organization arrested and police looking for you.<br /> 3-Large Criminal organizations will operate beyond the scope of the kindred's domain and other vampires will not appreciate your agents in their territory. With smaller groups, given gang rivalries, dealing with criminals will earn you the ire of other vampires who may also be involved in criminal doings.<br /> 4-A lot of big money items like drugs or human traficking require complicated networks.<br /> 5-Big Mafias have their own internal hunter teams because they're aware of the BS.<br /> 6-Camarilla Kindred don't want to look aggressive or ambitious. They're the sect that promotes quiet friendly gatherings, peace and prosperity, and the road of humanity. Most don't want to befriend a thug they can't control.</div> </div> </div> </div>That covers many of the reasons I experienced myself and with other players. In the majority of cases, they had a resource basis built on legal ventures or white collar crime, while street level stuff was reserved for emergencies when a quick infusion or specific item was needed.<br /> <br /> I think Sect and Clan also factor into it. In most cases a sire doesn't kick their new childe into the streets to fend for themselves, but will tutor them until they feel they are ready. That will tie a neonate to the resources of their sire and their Clan, which happens mostly off-screen when you decide the Backgrounds in chargen.<br /> Most Giovanni and Setite characters I have met had at least a toe in large scale drug dealing and money laundry, while Ventrue and Lasombra stuck to white collar stuff. Gangrel, Malks, and Nosferatu were for the most part happy with a low money / high contacts style of play. Tremere tended to access resources of their Clan, their idea of resources is a bit different. If they needed a quick fix of money, they usually sold magic favors to the moneybags.<br /> The most street level crime I've seen came from Caitiff, Brujah, Tzimis, and maybe somewhat surprisingly Toreador.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T05:21:58-07:00","id":1516093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources#post1516054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In VTM, a common trait is that the Elders have all the power/money and the young have none. My issue is that very few Neonates seem to capitalize on their inherent supernatural abilities to gain power/resources using crime.<br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> However, you almost never see neonates capitalizing on it.<br /> <br /> Why is that?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Advancibng in and improving mundane skills, capabilities, and methods is very often the default and normal way for starting out and / or young supernatural beings and magical persons ( including of course Vampires, Ghouls, and Revenants ) to establish themselves. Special abilities and supernatural powers definitely help, but it has to be noted that for example social networking or seeking wisdom and lore are also key and important priorities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T05:54:30-07:00","id":1516096,"title":"","content":"I am not scared of PC's having a lot of money/power. In my current game one of them started as a weapon industry magnate with Resources 5 and Influence 4. <br /> The game is still highly interesting, you just need to adapt the challenges and the scope of the conflicts (it has been really funny when he has tried to go toe to toe with Ballard for control of the steel industry)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T11:25:22-07:00","id":1516113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1516067#post1516067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creativity is indeed a key factor here<br /> (Or, I dare say, background knowledge, may God have mercy of the soul of a poor ST who have players with knowledge and background and let say path of conjuring or alchemy... )\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it make me a masochistic ST when I look forward to Players with that sort of enhanced play potential or does that make me a sadistic ST because with the Players bringing their A game to the table, I can bring all my knowledge and background in to counter balance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T11:37:38-07:00","id":1516114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1516062#post1516062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, the excuse I was given was that any neonate that draws attention to itself suddenly tends to have a short unlife, either because it attracted hunters or interfered with an older kindred's business, either way I guess that could happen if an ST give players a chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>The don't draw attention to yourself is common sense, but truth be told I have seen several STs jump the gun on what attracts attention.<br /> <br /> For instance, let's say you are a Gangrel Thief character, you don't want to hurt anyone, and you steal only from people or institutions that won't suffer terribly from the loss. You use Protean to allow you access to impossible routes for human sized creatures, crawling around as a bat or in mist form. If the thing being stolen is small enough to be carried, then you can just use the same method to leave. Alternatively using Animalism to get local rats or birds to bring you what you want is also a good method.<br /> <br /> Unless you do something stupid like shapeshifting in front of a Security Camera or leaving Protean claw marks in the vault door, then there is no reasonable way a Hunter or rival vampire would suspect vampiric activity in the first place. Most people suspect an inside job before they make the leap to supernatural involvement.<br /> <br /> Some STs are almost impatient for the PCs to attract attention so they can start their preplanned story, rather than letting the players dictate when things kick off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T12:38:22-07:00","id":1516121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1516062#post1516062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, the excuse I was given was that any neonate that draws attention to itself suddenly tends to have a short unlife, either because it attracted hunters or interfered with an older kindred's business, either way I guess that could happen if an ST give players a chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I forgot that some ST's probably dont want there games to go down that route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T15:19:44-07:00","id":1516133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1516114#post1516114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The don't draw attention to yourself is common sense, but truth be told I have seen several STs jump the gun on what attracts attention.<br /> <br /> For instance, let's say you are a Gangrel Thief character, you don't want to hurt anyone, and you steal only from people or institutions that won't suffer terribly from the loss. You use Protean to allow you access to impossible routes for human sized creatures, crawling around as a bat or in mist form. If the thing being stolen is small enough to be carried, then you can just use the same method to leave. Alternatively using Animalism to get local rats or birds to bring you what you want is also a good method.<br /> <br /> Unless you do something stupid like shapeshifting in front of a Security Camera or leaving Protean claw marks in the vault door, then there is no reasonable way a Hunter or rival vampire would suspect vampiric activity in the first place. Most people suspect an inside job before they make the leap to supernatural involvement.<br /> <br /> Some STs are almost impatient for the PCs to attract attention so they can start their preplanned story, rather than letting the players dictate when things kick off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without wanting to be boring but already being, if the institution in question has cameras it will be a bit complicated for you to enter in the form of a mist and you will have to get rid of it in some point, as far as I know, and small animals taking anything IS suspicious, in this case it's better to use a dog or monkey that can be trained (and if you don't worry about the risk of being known to be stealing), the other cases just as a distraction.<br /> <br /> Protean would be more useful to transform into a mouse or other small animal to map the place, know where the exits are, guard rounds, camera locations, these things, another option is to use this to sneak in a bag or luggage, and you could even use a famulus for that, but it's up to the ST whether an animal can memorize all of this and still be able to describe it to you. As a last resort, you can use it on an escape.<br /> <br /> Having said that, you must be thinking that this is all exaggeration and it is, although not that much IMO.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T15:29:32-07:00","id":1516135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1516133#post1516133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without wanting to be boring but already being, if the institution in question has cameras it will be a bit complicated for you to enter in the form of a mist and you will have to get rid of it in some point, as far as I know, and small animals taking anything IS suspicious, in this case it's better to use a dog or monkey that can be trained (and if you don't worry about the risk of being known to be stealing), the other cases just as a distraction.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Since most walk-in vaults have air vents as a safety measure, you can just mist form through the less than human sized air ducts. It is very rare to have an internal vault camera system. But pre-job recon is part of the game, so there really shouldn't be too many surprises when it comes to the target's security.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you can just ask a pack of rats to chew through any wires they come across, if you do this for a couple of weeks, all the false alarms and power outages can mask your actual robbery. As a side note, as someone who has had to clear out rat nests and seen what magpies collect, it really isn't that unusual for the animals to abscond with all sorts of goodies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T15:32:26-07:00","id":1516136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1516135#post1516135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since most walk-in vaults have air vents as a safety measure, you can just mist form through the less than human sized air ducts. It is very rare to have an internal vault camera system. But pre-job recon is part of the game, so there really shouldn't be too many surprises when it comes to the target's security.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, you can just ask a pack of rats to chew through any wires they come across, if you do this for a couple of weeks, all the false alarms and power outages can mask your actual robbery. As a side note, as someone who has had to clear out rat nests and seen what magpies collect, it really isn't that unusual for the animals to abscond with all sorts of goodies.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a good plan, but I wonder if the ST is going to let you wait weeks, worse he can make up that the rats don't want to do that anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T17:44:41-07:00","id":1516161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1516136#post1516136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a good plan, but I wonder if the ST is going to let you wait weeks, worse he can make up that the rats don't want to do that anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the nice part about having the rats do it is you can just drop by the target location and unleash the rats on their mission and leave. So you don't have to spend the entire night doing this. As far as the rats not wanting to do it, giving them some yummy food afterwards is not exactly a difficult trade to work out.<br /> <br /> I do feel that the idea of time is an odd concept in RPGs, especially in Vampire and Exalted. The characters have functionally unlimited lifespans so if a plan takes a week or two to come to fruition, its not like anyone is going to die of old age in the meantime. Likewise it isn't difficult for the ST to handwave a week passing and everyone involved makes a couple rolls for how things turned out.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the groups I played with were abnormal, but it wasn't uncommon to have a nightly story, a building story (aforementioned sabotage plan), and then the overarching campaign story going on simultaneously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T17:54:34-07:00","id":1516163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1516161#post1516161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well the nice part about having the rats do it is you can just drop by the target location and unleash the rats on their mission and leave. So you don't have to spend the entire night doing this. As far as the rats not wanting to do it, giving them some yummy food afterwards is not exactly a difficult trade to work out.<br /> <br /> I do feel that the idea of time is an odd concept in RPGs, especially in Vampire and Exalted. The characters have functionally unlimited lifespans so if a plan takes a week or two to come to fruition, its not like anyone is going to die of old age in the meantime. Likewise it isn't difficult for the ST to handwave a week passing and everyone involved makes a couple rolls for how things turned out.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the groups I played with were abnormal, but it wasn't uncommon to have a nightly story, a building story (aforementioned sabotage plan), and then the overarching campaign story going on simultaneously.</div> </div> </div> </div>I particularly find it strange, because if you stop to think about it, vampires need to replace blood, garous fury, faith fallen and so on if weeks go by, you think that these values will change, so that's where things get a little strange, Of course, you can reveal it to the game, but this is liable to generate complaints.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T20:50:49-07:00","id":1516171,"title":"","content":"The big problem with criminal activity is that the longer you're at it, and the more successful you are, eventually you're going to come up on the radar of law enforcement. This will be local police, but eventually it will include Federal agencies. Rats chew through wires and then someone robs a bank and a bunch of money goes missing? Yeah, the FBI is going to be all over that. Whatever ends up happening, that could end up being a a significant Masquerade Breach. The rewards are great, but the risks can snowball pretty quickly. Generally speaking this is why the Camarilla tends not to truck too much with the criminal underworld. For the most part it's the Independent Clans (the Giovanni and the Followers of Set) that have the biggest presence in the underworld. Among the Camarilla, only the Brujah tended to engage much with criminal elements, and then it was often the Anarch wing of the Clan.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that the Camarilla <i>never</i> engages with criminals, but members would be encouraged to keep such interactions at a distance and short term rather than getting too caught up in that sort of lifestyle. If a vampire starts risking drawing the attention of Federal law enforcement (especially in V5 with the Second Inquisition) the Camarilla would quickly move to force the vampire to cut those ties - either by faking a death or just outright killing the vampire for the risk of drawing that sort of heat to the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-25-2023, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T00:48:06-07:00","id":1516185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources#post1516054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In VTM, a common trait is that the Elders have all the power/money and the young have none. My issue is that very few Neonates seem to capitalize on their inherent supernatural abilities to gain power/resources using crime.<br /> <br /> Presence and Dominate can be used quite easily to form a criminal organization/gang, force mortals into giving you what you want, and to scare mortals into not moving against you. Auspex can alert you to the movement of law enforcement and victims, as well as help you obtain important information like the code to the safe where jewelers keep their most valuable items. In fact, every discipline can be used in some way to easily commit crimes that mortals would have serious trouble pulling off.<br /> <br /> However, you almost never see neonates capitalizing on it.<br /> <br /> Why is that?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on whatever group you're hanging with because it's pretty common for the Anarch groups I belong to, to have the players come from criminal organizations. However, I should note that you've actually just described the problem AND the solution.<br /> <br /> Neonate: Hey, I'm going to rob three banks.<br /> <br /> ST: You get all of the loot.<br /> <br /> Neonate: What, really?<br /> <br /> ST: As much as you can carry off. It goes off without a hitch. Now a bunch of ghouls and the Sheriff show up at your haven.<br /> <br /> Neonate: What, why?<br /> <br /> ST: Because you didn't ask permission to rob banks under Al Capone. They're also Ballard's banks.<br /> <br /> EVERYTHING is someone's territory in the big city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T07:23:21-07:00","id":1516209,"title":"","content":"<br /> Neonates don't need to do anything high profile like that. Find a lonely but otherwise successful person, blood bond them (ideally without their knowledge) live in their home and use their money.<br /> There's a lot of reasons why this isn't always a great idea, but it's good and discrete enough for anyone going through a difficult time. Any neonate regardless of clan can manage this. While you're doing that, you can prepare for something better.<br /> <br /> <i>N:So aunt, this is your best friend that you live with. Why doesn't she have her own bed? Don't tell me she sleeps on the couch.<br /> A: Of course she doesn't sleep on the couch, there's a hidden alcove in the basement under the stairs, whoops I wasn't supposed to say that. Suppose I have other nephews. Do you wanna go swimming?</i><br /> <br /> If robbery's your hobby? That's fine, but Big Banks are too high profile You'll want local branches, jewellery stores, small businesses, houses... great stuff.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T09:15:04-07:00","id":1516218,"title":"","content":"I like that idea MYWifeIsScary. That would be an ideal first step in a Neonate journey to make a comfortable existence, the only downside could be is that an Ancilla or Elder might have a vested interest in certain mortals and wouldn't want some whelp poaching on there domian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T09:22:27-07:00","id":1516220,"title":"","content":"In regards to the original post. Most neonates probably came from law abiding backgrounds and tried not to hangout with known criminals and would be to nervous to start doing it right away and with certain clever uses of the disciplines as an option. You may not need to go that route at all at first if ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T10:30:45-07:00","id":1516225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1516185#post1516185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on whatever group you're hanging with because it's pretty common for the Anarch groups I belong to, to have the players come from criminal organizations. However, I should note that you've actually just described the problem AND the solution.<br /> <br /> Neonate: Hey, I'm going to rob three banks.<br /> <br /> ST: You get all of the loot.<br /> <br /> Neonate: What, really?<br /> <br /> ST: As much as you can carry off. It goes off without a hitch. Now a bunch of ghouls and the Sheriff show up at your haven.<br /> <br /> Neonate: What, why?<br /> <br /> ST: Because you didn't ask permission to rob banks under Al Capone. They're also Ballard's banks.<br /> <br /> EVERYTHING is someone's territory in the big city.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would shy away from robbing banks and focus more on stuff like robbing convenience stores and jewelry stores, low-profile stuff. I get what you mean though, however, at the same time, I highly doubt that a majority of businesses are going to be run by vampires. Like yeah, they may get pissed that you're doing it in their domain, but I highly doubt they own every single business in it. And depending on whose territory it is, the criminal lick in question could strike a deal with the domain holder in which they kick up a percentage of the profits in return for them not making a fuss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T10:47:18-07:00","id":1516229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1516171#post1516171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The big problem with criminal activity is that the longer you're at it, and the more successful you are, eventually you're going to come up on the radar of law enforcement. This will be local police, but eventually it will include Federal agencies. Rats chew through wires and then someone robs a bank and a bunch of money goes missing? Yeah, the FBI is going to be all over that. Whatever ends up happening, that could end up being a a significant Masquerade Breach. The rewards are great, but the risks can snowball pretty quickly. Generally speaking this is why the Camarilla tends not to truck too much with the criminal underworld. For the most part it's the Independent Clans (the Giovanni and the Followers of Set) that have the biggest presence in the underworld. Among the Camarilla, only the Brujah tended to engage much with criminal elements, and then it was often the Anarch wing of the Clan.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that the Camarilla <i>never</i> engages with criminals, but members would be encouraged to keep such interactions at a distance and short term rather than getting too caught up in that sort of lifestyle. If a vampire starts risking drawing the attention of Federal law enforcement (especially in V5 with the Second Inquisition) the Camarilla would quickly move to force the vampire to cut those ties - either by faking a death or just outright killing the vampire for the risk of drawing that sort of heat to the area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something I failed to mention in my initial post was that there seems to be a suprising lack of kindered who could be robbing a couple places/committing a few scams and frauds, and then going legit after making enough money to invest in themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T11:07:23-07:00","id":1516233,"title":"","content":"Very few of us are real life Moriaty from Sherlock Holmes and we can be quite sloppy in regards in such matters. That why law enforcement have such a saying of &quot;Thank god for dumb criminals.&quot; and as pointed out that certain disciplines could be used to obtain resources and a decent haven without having to resort to criminal actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T12:19:04-07:00","id":1516239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1516233#post1516233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very few of us are real life Moriaty from Sherlock Holmes and we can be quite sloppy in regards in such matters. That why law enforcement have such a saying of &quot;Thank god for dumb criminals.&quot; and as pointed out that certain disciplines could be used to obtain resources and a decent haven without having to resort to criminal actions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont think one needs to be a Moriarty to be competent at crime tbh. IDK if you have ever heard of Larry Lawton, but in some videos/podcasts he has featured in, he rates how realistic some jewel store/bank robbery movies are and breaks down what mistakes they made and actually explains how he commited his hiests. If you look on his wikipedia page you can also see how he was caught. What Im trying to get at, is that the internet can actually teach someone on how commit and get away with crimes. Now Im not saying its going to turn you into a criminal mastermind, but it is a starting off point.<br /> <br /> Regarding law enforcement, I have heard of situations, mainly online, on how police are at times unwilling to go after criminals who have commited break ins and the such. So depending on what you actually steal and how often you do it in a certain area, the police may not be willing to do much. I could be wrong though.<br /> <br /> I do get what you are saying though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 06-26-2023, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T12:32:16-07:00","id":1516242,"title":"","content":"I think a part of why crime gets associated with neonates is that it makes sense thematically with what we\u2019re told about the general relations of elders and neonates towards resources and influence: there is a scarcity of resources and the elders (and ancillae) have had the time to bogart those resources and the \u2018legitimate levers of power\u2019 (government, media, finance, major corporations, police, etc.) and all that\u2019s left for the neonates is to either scrabble for crumbs from their elders or to carve out a niche for themselves in the illegitimate world (crime).<br /> <br /> I think one of the issues that comes with that is that there is a struggle for STs to portray that dynamic of scarcity and hegemony of the elders in play. It\u2019s one thing to say that all the major levers of power have been claimed by the local elders and ancillae but in reality the clever neonate can probably get their way to 5 resources even if limited to a select number of small businesses and interest in the C-list financial institutions that are too small and numerous for older vampires to have claimed them all. This means that, if played that way, even the average neonate within a traditional Camarilla domain can establish themselves in tremendous material comfort without needing to resort to the world of underworld finance. The only reason then for the typical neonate-anarch criminal archetype to take shape then is if they either can\u2019t use legitimate avenues or they simply choose not to, whether out of arbitrary pique or a willful rejection of the establishment. <br /> <br /> Now I don\u2019t think the above is necessarily the only way to run it. I can imagine a careful ST combining geographical carving and allocation to create a situation where a young vampire is forced to either bend the knee or to become a de facto outlaw to get a leg-up and I think that would create an interesting setting, perhaps one more faithful to the intent of the first edition game, but I don\u2019t think it\u2019s the only way either.<br /> <br /> The well-designed scarcity on the one hand creates a setting where the neonates either accept submission and chafe under the yoke in order to gain power or they accept the mantle of anarch and combine poaching, raiding, and criminality to carve out their own niche (which interestingly means that even as the Anarchs must be suppressed the elders probably have a greater respect for the Anarchs than they do the loyalists). On the other hand the less high-pressure high-scarcity domains allow those who are willing to play the game to gain a comfortable position with relative ease - the tensions then become one of a relative difference. What does it matter that you have 5 Resources if you still only have 1-2 Status and all the best domains are still under the control of the elders? This could create another interesting setting where a significant section of young vampires are satisfied to retreat into their own private concerns, some drop out of society entirely, but an ambitious few yearn for the opportunity to overthrow enough of their elders to gain a bigger piece of the pie. This could create a situation not unlike how Chicago by Night is depicted in early books.<br /> <br /> Honestly, after some thought, I could imagine these as not being contradictory but rather a spectrum. A \u2018healthy\u2019 vampiric domain resembles the latter case where scarcity is relatively low and their is enough free resources available to buy off a section of the young licks and to keep either the ambitious or the Anarchs from gaining a significant section of followers. A \u2018dangerous\u2019 vampiric domain could resemble the former case where scarcity is relatively high and the young vampires must either enter society as toadies to gain advancement or reject society entirely and adopt the anarch ways (somewhat like how Denver comes off in that one early adventure book, Alien Ways iirc).<br /> <br /> These are just my two cents on how a consideration of setting based on first principles could effect the answers one comes to from a question like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T13:22:22-07:00","id":1516247,"title":"","content":"Most PCs who want such a criminal empire is going to establish that Backgrounds - buying the appropriate Influence, Allies, Retainers, etc. (justified in some way, and their Disciplines can be part of that) and have it operated in the background.<br /> <br /> In general, players want to spend their time at the game table on things that cannot be established through Backgrounds. They want face time with other vampires, supernatural forces, roleplay with humans in their immediate circle, work on the ST plot, investigate chronicle mysteries or groups in the setting, and so on. In contrast, roleplaying through the minutiae of building up their &quot;empire&quot; from scratch either does not interest them, challenge them, or divert from things that are more fun. It's a distraction.<br /> <br /> I can think of plenty of exceptions, but I believe most players (at least in a table top experience, I know Online gamesn or any games that allow for extensive bluebooking, can be very different) want to use their limited time at the game table differently.<br /> <br /> However, I do admit that is can be trivially easy for vampires to get anything they would want from mortals. They just need to do it in a way that does not attract much attention or threaten the Masquerade (not even necessarily through committing a crime). A lot of vampires probably survive that way on a day to day basis. And sometimes PCs overlook such solutions, or overcomplicate such things. Or the ST is too inexperienced to prepare for such solutions or deal with them to problems they intended as challenges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T14:59:59-07:00","id":1516261,"title":"","content":"I'm aware of Lawton and his channel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T23:29:26-07:00","id":1516321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1516225#post1516225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would shy away from robbing banks and focus more on stuff like robbing convenience stores and jewelry stores, low-profile stuff. I get what you mean though, however, at the same time, I highly doubt that a majority of businesses are going to be run by vampires. Like yeah, they may get pissed that you're doing it in their domain, but I highly doubt they own every single business in it. And depending on whose territory it is, the criminal lick in question could strike a deal with the domain holder in which they kick up a percentage of the profits in return for them not making a fuss.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, nothing is stopping robbing convenience stores for petty cash but it's also a pretty small use of one's time as a vampire. There's plenty of other ways to also make bank as a vampire:<br /> <br /> * Ghoul someone who is already rich.<br /> * Presence to make people want to invest in your MLM business<br /> * Dominate to simply get people to give you money<br /> * Be willing to work for a rich vampire in exchange for a steady income (AKA How the Camarilla works as a Pyramid Scheme)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T01:38:24-07:00","id":1516417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1516321#post1516321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, nothing is stopping robbing convenience stores for petty cash but it's also a pretty small use of one's time as a vampire. There's plenty of other ways to also make bank as a vampire:<br /> <br /> * Ghoul someone who is already rich.<br /> * Presence to make people want to invest in your MLM business<br /> * Dominate to simply get people to give you money<br /> * Be willing to work for a rich vampire in exchange for a steady income (AKA How the Camarilla works as a Pyramid Scheme)</div> </div> </div> </div>There is also stealing and theft of very special and precious items and goods. Within this there is also pssobility of taking or seizing items that are considered to be desirable locally or by particular persons.<br /> <br /> On a wider scale, there is also the possiblity of exploting or robbing groups and companies. And of course there is also seizing or stealing of mysteries, knowledge, secrets, and methods. If these can be stolen or taken at all, that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T06:03:59-07:00","id":1516444,"title":"","content":"One aspect which I think influences why neonates don't get fabolously successful very quick is how predatory Elders are. If you run the Elders as conservative model citizens then, yes, many tactics to give neonates fast power and riches would work.<br /> <br /> But if you run Elders, as I've come to understand how they operate &quot;in universe&quot;, then there's two very possible outcomes for a neonate reaching success. Only possibly mitigated by having sufficient contacts and such in the influential (aka Kindred Elders) local population.<br /> <br /> 1. An Elder sweeps in and takes the stuff from the neonate. That's predatory behavior if I ever saw one and vampires are supposed to be pretty predatory.<br /> <br /> 2. One or more Elders might think that this young neonate could, in their paranoid minds, become a problem or a threat due to talent and such. Thus they kill the neonate.<br /> <br /> I think that many GMs play the Elders, for gameplay reasons, to be essentially benevolent, understanding and respecful towards younger Kindred. Yes, some neonates can absoluely fight back if the Elders would screw with them. These neonates get targeted for elimination early in their unlives before they can gain the proper means to fight back against the Elders.<br /> <br /> Thus my understanding is that alot of neonates who has considerble talent simply have to play worse than they can in order to not stand out and get targeted by the older, less human, Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":970,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","user":"Gurkhal","date":".  The first post was written in some pretty bad English, so I've gone over the post and hopefully make it somewhat more readable 06-28-2023, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T06:21:53-07:00","id":1516450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1516321#post1516321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, nothing is stopping robbing convenience stores for petty cash but it's also a pretty small use of one's time as a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a player whose Tremere character robbed gas stations as a hobby (and usually without the use of his Disciplines), simply for the kick of excitement. It's a valid alternative motivation for vampires to commit crimes; the Embrace kills a lot of the usual options to get your rush on.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T09:11:42-07:00","id":1516468,"title":"","content":"I'd would go with ghouling somebody who is quite wealthy and use there homes as a good haven myself. I'd would want to make sure that I didn't get an elder or ancilla who already have a vested interest in that person on my case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":".  Simple fleshing out of a statement. 06-28-2023, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T12:44:45-07:00","id":1516513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1516468#post1516468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd would go with ghouling somebody who is quite wealthy and use there homes as a good haven myself. I'd would want to make sure that I didn't get an elder or ancilla who already have a vested interest in that person.</div> </div> </div> </div>A while back on reddit someone asked how to deal with the Second Inquisition in their charachters area, a user commented that they should blood bond the SI agent, and turn his family into slaves and make a profit off of them. Lets just say that their suggestions for how to specifically make money off of them was kinda dark.<br /> <br /> Something that made me chuckle, was how they ended it by saying something like &quot;But dont kill them! What are we? Animals?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Definitely Camarilla behaviour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 06-28-2023, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T12:57:23-07:00","id":1516515,"title":"","content":"Players just generally don't want to do that sort of thing. Some players want to be rich, so they buy high backgrounds on character-creation, and then live out the fantasy of holding lavish parties where they sip blood from wineglasses and have catty conversations with other party-goers. No need for a lot of criminal activity in that case. You see a lot of Toreador mains doing this.<br /> <br /> Others want to live out the fantasy of being a savage monster. They want to sleep earthmelded and pounce on people in alleyways. Money actually gets in the way of that fantasy, making living the way you want to fantasize living into a sort of plot-hole. You see a lot of Gangrel mains doing this. Doing things like taking the No Haven flaw and absolutely never buying it off.<br /> <br /> There's really not much call for doing this sort of thing. Character creation allows you to bypass it, and those who don't bypass it generally don't want it in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T13:22:05-07:00","id":1516520,"title":"","content":"Requiem guy here, but I'm rather surprised to hear that (generally) players don't seem to commit crimes with their vampire powers. Because (Giovanni/Hecata jokes aside), being a vampire seems a lot like already being in a mob:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The tradition of Masquerade is a lot like Omerta; &quot;We don't talk about this thing of ours...&quot;</li> <li>The traditions of Progeny or Accountability remind me of Donnie Brasco. &quot;Nobody can touch you, because I represent you.&quot;</li> <li>The Camarilla (and it's Requiem counterpart, the Invictus) seem a lot like the Cosa Nostra or Five Families, with Princes and Primogen acting like Dons and Capos.</li> </ol>Sorry if I'm being Captain Obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T13:26:31-07:00","id":1516521,"title":"","content":"I mean I think most vampire games involve characters doing things which would be by definition criminal, particularly in maintenance of the Masquerade (the vampiric Omert\u00e0), but tbh I think a larger part of this discussion is that many players and STs have little to no interest in dealing with the practical logistics of feeding, domain, resources and influence in game; they\u2019re happy to let the dots handle that while they do whatever it is they prefer to be doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T14:31:48-07:00","id":1516527,"title":"","content":"Fun little trick with movement of the mind is to unlock things with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T16:25:06-07:00","id":1516550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1516513#post1516513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A while back on reddit someone asked how to deal with the Second Inquisition in their charachters area, a user commented that they should blood bond the SI agent, and turn his family into slaves and make a profit off of them. Lets just say that their suggestions for how to specifically make money off of them was kinda dark.<br /> <br /> Something that made me chuckle, was how they ended it by saying something like &quot;But dont kill them! What are we? Animals?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Definitely Camarilla behaviour.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is so dark and twisted and I love it and should mention it in our game and see if we can use it in our intelligence gathering coterie without damaging our humanity ratings to much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T16:08:16-07:00","id":1516922,"title":"","content":"So, any Neonate, that doesn't commit any crimes to obtain wealth and power, is a neonate that doesn't rock the boat and is a Neonate that's going to live to be an Ancilla-vampire as long as the Elders are concerned; they like those kind of vampires. <br /> <br /> In my games, my players will commit crimes all the time to the point it's not just a mortal-problem, but a kindred-problem. One time, I had to create an entire police-force of NPCs to track them down. Don't kill police-officers. <br /> <br /> And it's not the Elders with the wealth and power; sure, they have it, but they are aloof and don't seem to concerned with acquiring more of it. It's the Ancilla that are at the peak of their wealth, and the Neonates that always seem to flaunt it. Ancilla are slowly becoming detached with their wealth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T16:45:02-07:00","id":1516927,"title":"","content":"I'm also surprised to hear players aren't doing more of this stuff. I assumed it was a major default playstyle, since the game is already so much like a crime drama. I've yet to run a game in the current edition where the players didn't want be a fang gang. Hell, even when I was but a youth, our childish games of Vampire consisted largely of gangsters and hooligans, with gothic romance being more of a sauce than a main course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T15:43:44-07:00","id":1517010,"title":"","content":"Some stuff I've seen or heard about.<br /> <br /> Fun crime combo in a Sabbat game a few years back a lasombra teamed up with a tzmisce for pimping. The tzmisce would use flesh crafting to make the prostitutes exceptionally attractive and robust employees. The lasombra used Dominate to ensure they didn't recall not being app 5...and that their boss was a vampire.<br /> <br /> A Tremere who would use expedient paperwork for white collar crime. He'd take bribes to get things through city Hall.<br /> <br /> Giovanni using necromancy for blackmail<br /> <br /> Toreador antitribu body mod exhibitionist/extreme cosmetics. Think American Mary but with viscitude.<br /> <br /> A setite who'd use obfuscate to show up as whoever you desire for escorting/prostitution.<br /> <br /> Assamite high value thief pretty much all their disciplines where good for this.<br /> <br /> Sabbat lasombra who would use a hoody and obtenerbration to go nazgul when robbing places<br /> <br /> Bonus non vampire- order of hermes who'd use matter 2 to transmute expensive high end meds and sell them cheap as back ally doc....pretty altruistic overall. Eventually he moves into back ally surgery by using mind get a medicane 5 in a month then developed life to ensure he was providing millionaire teer surgery for about a 100 bucks.<br /> <br /> <br /> edit-and as always be sure to Rob the people you kill as it provides a low level masquarade defence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-02-2023, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T16:47:03-07:00","id":1517011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1517010#post1517010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some stuff I've seen or heard about.<br /> <br /> Giovanni using necromancy for blackmail</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's so safe, ghosts make good spies, but blackmail needs some proof, photo or recording, otherwise he can just deny everything, I suppose you can dribble this problem with subterfurge, but here's the tip.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1517010#post1517010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Toreador antitribu body mod exhibitionist/extreme cosmetics. Think American Mary but with viscitude.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it works best as an example of a prostitute or a model in this case, maybe as a bargaining chip too, or you can offer these services in exchange for favors and if the guy refuses you can lie saying you can undo it with a snap of your fingers , and yes it would be easier to make him a ghoul, but there are certain things a ghoul cannot do. But your idea is not bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1517010#post1517010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A setite who'd use obfuscate to show up as whoever you desire for escorting/prostitution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Setites get money through blackmail and favors, some own establishments where mortals satisfy their most forbidden desires and even where they let secrets slip, like in bars, universities. They also sell drugs, blood and even information, there is a Setite sorcery that makes anything abnormally addictive which helps a lot, they also promote illegal fights and according to a character concept this is also used to select future Setites from the warrior caste who later even serve as bodyguards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1517010#post1517010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assamite high value thief pretty much all their disciplines where good for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, the Assamites sometimes work as assassins for hire, kidnapping, fighting in guerrillas, transporting weapons, infiltrators and even spies, this to have money for their operations, keep their skills sharp and also as a way to obtain contacts and various resources. , but I imagine they must steal something during their missions.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T17:11:57-07:00","id":1517013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1517011#post1517011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it's so safe, ghosts make good spies, but blackmail needs some proof, photo or recording, otherwise he can just deny everything, I suppose you can dribble this problem with subterfurge, but here's the tip.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think it works best as an example of a prostitute or a model in this case, maybe as a bargaining chip too, or you can offer these services in exchange for favors and if the guy refuses you can lie saying you can undo it with a snap of your fingers , and yes it would be easier to make him a ghoul, but there are certain things a ghoul cannot do. But your idea is not bad.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Setites get money through blackmail and favors, some own establishments where mortals satisfy their most forbidden desires and even where they let secrets slip, like in bars, universities. They also sell drugs, blood and even information, there is a Setite sorcery that makes anything abnormally addictive which helps a lot, they also promote illegal fights and according to a character concept this is also used to select future Setites from the warrior caste who later even serve as bodyguards.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As far as I know, the Assamites sometimes work as assassins for hire, kidnapping, fighting in guerrillas, transporting weapons, infiltrators and even spies, this to have money for their operations, keep their skills sharp and also as a way to obtain contacts and various resources. , but I imagine they must steal something during their missions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He wasn't genrally using them as spies more &quot;so who killed you? Or &quot;tell me your friends and loved ones darkest secrets.&quot; Which gives you a lot to work with.<br /> <br /> american mary style modification isnt conventional and is often immoral and illegal, for example two clients wanted to be 'merged'. As I recall she took her obligations to her clients seriously and would honour their requests, she'd provide full reversal if clients where unhappy but no refunds.<br /> <br /> Brrrrr<br /> <br /> Those are certainly angles for acquisition of wealth but he seemed content with his angle. I can see certain advantages vs using magic heroin","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-02-2023, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T00:11:46-07:00","id":1517036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1517011#post1517011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it's so safe, ghosts make good spies, but blackmail needs some proof, photo or recording, otherwise he can just deny everything, I suppose you can dribble this problem with subterfurge, but here's the tip.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think it works best as an example of a prostitute or a model in this case, maybe as a bargaining chip too, or you can offer these services in exchange for favors and if the guy refuses you can lie saying you can undo it with a snap of your fingers , and yes it would be easier to make him a ghoul, but there are certain things a ghoul cannot do. But your idea is not bad.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Setites get money through blackmail and favors, some own establishments where mortals satisfy their most forbidden desires and even where they let secrets slip, like in bars, universities. They also sell drugs, blood and even information, there is a Setite sorcery that makes anything abnormally addictive which helps a lot, they also promote illegal fights and according to a character concept this is also used to select future Setites from the warrior caste who later even serve as bodyguards.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As far as I know, the Assamites sometimes work as assassins for hire, kidnapping, fighting in guerrillas, transporting weapons, infiltrators and even spies, this to have money for their operations, keep their skills sharp and also as a way to obtain contacts and various resources. , but I imagine they must steal something during their missions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>He wasn't genrally using them as spies more &quot;so who killed you? Or &quot;tell me your friends and loved ones darkest secrets.&quot; Which gives you a lot to work with.<br /> <br /> <br /> american mary style modification isnt conventional and is often immoral and illegal, for example two clients wanted to be 'merged'. As I recall she took her obligations to her clients seriously and would honour their requests, she'd provide full reversal if clients where unhappy but no refunds.<br /> <br /> Brrrrr<br /> <br /> That said conventional cosmetic enhancements using viss is an obvious angle for cash.<br /> <br /> Those are certainly angles for acquisition of wealth but he seemed content with his angle. I can see certain advantages vs using magic heroin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T09:03:19-07:00","id":1517077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1516054-thoughts-regarding-neonates-not-exploiting-crime-to-obtain-power-resources?p=1516922#post1516922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, any Neonate, that doesn't commit any crimes to obtain wealth and power, is a neonate that doesn't rock the boat and is a Neonate that's going to live to be an Ancilla-vampire as long as the Elders are concerned; they like those kind of vampires.<br /> <br /> In my games, my players will commit crimes all the time to the point it's not just a mortal-problem, but a kindred-problem. One time, I had to create an entire police-force of NPCs to track them down. Don't kill police-officers.<br /> <br /> And it's not the Elders with the wealth and power; sure, they have it, but they are aloof and don't seem to concerned with acquiring more of it. It's the Ancilla that are at the peak of their wealth, and the Neonates that always seem to flaunt it. Ancilla are slowly becoming detached with their wealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention that the Ancilla are starting to begin to gain an understanding of what true power and what a discrete tool having wealth is and being to showy is a bad to gain attention that you don't need at this point.<br /> <br /> I keep in mind when I play these older characters is that they can do what they want, but do it in a way that doesn't endanger your lofty perch or get the prince annoyed and sending his or her agents to swoop in and bring some sort of order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}